## Ability Integration

### Progressive Ability Unlocks
- Design controls that evolve with player progression:
  1. **Basic Abilities**: Available from the start (tap = basic attack)
  2. **Movement Upgrades**: Enhance swipe gestures with dash, wall jump, etc.
  3. **Advanced Actions**: Transform hold-release into powerful charged attacks

### Ability Manager Integration

```javascript
// src/lib/game/abilities/ability-manager.js
export class AbilityManager {
  constructor(player) {
    this.player = player;
    this.unlockedAbilities = new Set();
    this.abilityModifiers = {};
    
    // Set up initial abilities
    this.initializeAbilities();
  }
  
  initializeAbilities() {
    // Define all abilities with their default state
    this.abilities = {
      // Movement abilities
      dash: {
        unlocked: false,
        cooldown: 1000, // ms
        lastUsed: 0,
        power: 1.0
      },
      doubleJump: {
        unlocked: false,
        usesPerAirTime: 1,
        usesRemaining: 0,
        power: 1.0
      },
      wallClimb: {
        unlocked: false,
        staminaCost: 10,
        climbSpeed: 1.0
      },
      
      // Combat abilities
      chargedAttack: {
        unlocked: false,
        minChargeTime: 500, // ms
        maxDamage: 3,
        radius: 1.0
      },
      groundPound: {
        unlocked: false,
        damage: 2,
        radius: 1.5,
        stunDuration: 1000 // ms
      }
    };
  }
  
  unlockAbility(abilityName) {
    if (this.abilities.hasOwnProperty(abilityName)) {
      this.abilities[abilityName].unlocked = true;
      this.unlockedAbilities.add(abilityName);
      
      // Reset any ability-specific counters
      if (abilityName === 'doubleJump') {
        this.resetDoubleJump();
      }
      
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
  
  isAbilityUnlocked(abilityName) {
    return this.abilities.hasOwnProperty(abilityName) && 
           this.abilities[abilityName].unlocked;
  }
  
  isAbilityReady(abilityName) {
    if (!this.isAbilityUnlocked(abilityName)) return false;
    
    const ability = this.abilities[abilityName];
    
    switch (abilityName) {
      case 'dash':
        return performance.now() - ability.lastUsed >= ability.cooldown;
        
      case 'doubleJump':
        return !this.player.onGround && ability.usesRemaining > 0;
        
      case 'wallClimb':
        return this.player.nearWall && this.player.stamina >= ability.staminaCost;
        
      case 'chargedAttack':
      case 'groundPound':
        return true; // Always available if unlocked
        
      default:
        return false;
    }
  }
  
  useAbility(abilityName, ...args) {
    if (!this.isAbilityReady(abilityName)) return false;
    
    const ability = this.abilities[abilityName];
    
    switch (abilityName) {
      case 'dash':
        ability.lastUsed = performance.now();
        this.player.performDash(...args);
        return true;
        
      case 'doubleJump':
        ability.usesRemaining--;
        this.player.performDoubleJump(...args);
        return true;
        
      case 'wallClimb':
        this.player.stamina -= ability.staminaCost;
        this.player.performWallClimb(...args);
        return true;
        
      case 'chargedAttack':
        this.player.performChargedAttack(...args);
        return true;
        
      case 'groundPound':
        this.player.performGroundPound(...args);
        return true;
        
      default:
        return false;
    }
  }
  
  resetDoubleJump() {
    const ability = this.abilities.doubleJump;
    if (ability.unlocked) {
      ability.usesRemaining = ability.usesPerAirTime;
    }
  }
  
  onPlayerLanded() {
    this.resetDoubleJump();
  }
  
  onPlayerWallContact(isInContact) {
    // Reset abilities when touching walls
    if (isInContact) {
      this.resetDoubleJump();
    }
  }
  
  update() {
    // Regenerate stamina, update cooldowns, etc.
    if (this.player.onGround) {
      this.player.stamina = Math.min(
        this.player.maxStamina, 
        this.player.stamina + this.player.staminaRegenRate
      );
    }
  }
}
```

## Mobile-Specific Optimizations

### Touch Precision Enhancements
- Implement a dynamic hit testing system that adjusts touch targets based on:
  - Screen size and density
  - Player capabilities
  - Environmental context

### Orientation Handling
- Support both portrait and landscape orientations:
  - Adjust control zones based on orientation
  - Preserve gameplay experience in both modes
  - Implement smooth transitions during orientation changes

### Touch Calibration
- Allow players to customize touch sensitivity:
  - Swipe distance thresholds
  - Hold duration thresholds
  - Control zone size/positioning

## Best Practices

1. **Performance**
   - Use passive event listeners where possible
   - Throttle/debounce touch event handling
   - Use requestAnimationFrame for visual feedback

2. **Accessibility**
   - Support alternate input methods (keyboard, gamepad)
   - Provide visual clarity for all touch interactions
   - Allow customization of touch sensitivity

3. **Browser Compatibility**
   - Test on multiple browsers and devices
   - Implement polyfills for missing touch APIs
   - Handle vendor-specific touch event differences

4. **Touch Issues Mitigation**
   - Include methods to cancel erroneous gestures
   - Implement touch exclusion zones for UI elements
   - Provide clear visual indication of valid touch areas

5. **Debugging**
   - Create a debug visualization for touch points and gestures
   - Log touch events for troubleshooting
   - Add performance monitoring for touch input responsiveness 